        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under nitrogen (drybox/Schlenk), Ce (0.140 g, 1.0 mmol), PhSeSePh (0.47 g, 1.5 mmol), and Hg (0.024 g, 0.11 mmol) were combined in THF (ca. 30 mL) and stirred until the metal was consumed (1 day), giving a yellow solution with a small amount of greenish-yellow solid. The solution was filtered and SeO2 (0.11 g, 1.0 mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred for 1 h at 55 °C, during which SeO2 dissolved to give a brownish-yellow solution that was filtered, reduced in volume under vacuum to ca. 15 mL, and layered with hexane (15 mL) to give yellow plate-shaped crystals.",
